# Windsurf Rules for SLM Fine-Tuning Project

## Context
ML fine-tuning project using PyTorch + Hugging Face. Focus on parameter-efficient fine-tuning of small language models (1B-7B parameters).

## Rules
- Use LoRA/QLoRA as default fine-tuning method.
- All training configs in YAML format under `configs/`.
- Scripts should accept `--config` flag pointing to YAML config.
- Always log training metrics (loss, learning rate, GPU memory).
- Include data validation steps before training starts.
- Use bf16 mixed precision on Ampere+ GPUs, fp16 otherwise.
- Set gradient accumulation to simulate larger effective batch sizes.
- Save optimizer state with checkpoints for training resumption.
- Test inference after training to verify model outputs.
- Pin all dependency versions in requirements.txt.
